  data: {
    LLM: "1. King of Trumps: If the turned-up card is a King, the dealer scores 1 point immediately. If a player holds the King of Trumps in their hand, they must declare it before the first trick to score 1 point.\n2. The Proposal: The nonnddealer (Elder Hand), if unhappy with their cards, can 'propose' to discard. If the dealer agrees, both players discard any number of cards and draw replacements from the deck. This can continue until the deck is empty or a proposal is refused.\n3. The Play: Standard trickndtaking. You MUST follow suit if possible and MUST win the trick (over-trump or over-play) if you are able.",
    Player: "1. King of Trumps: If the turned-up card is a King, the dealer scores 1 point immediately. If a player holds the King of Trumps in their hand, they must declare it before the first trick to score 1 point.\n2. The Proposal: The nonnddealer (Elder Hand), if unhappy with their cards, can 'propose' to discard. If the dealer agrees, both players discard any number of cards and draw replacements from the deck. This can continue until the deck is empty or a proposal is refused.\n3. The Play: Standard trickndtaking. You MUST follow suit if possible and MUST win the trick (over-trump or over-play) if you are able.",
    objective: 'Win at least three tricks to score points. The first player to reach 5 points wins the game.',
    gameplay: "1. King of Trumps: If the turned-up card is a King, the dealer scores 1 point immediately. If a player holds the King of Trumps in their hand, they must declare it before the first trick to score 1 point.\n2. The Proposal: The nonnddealer (Elder Hand), if unhappy with their cards, can 'propose' to discard. If the dealer agrees, both players discard any number of cards and draw replacements from the deck. This can continue until the deck is empty or a proposal is refused.\n3. The Play: Standard trickndtaking. You MUST follow suit if possible and MUST win the trick (over-trump or over-play) if you are able.",
